devops.workflows could observe the cloud repo and start a workflow in it.
It could not steer one, could not see any other repo, and could not stop
or retry anything. Every gap below was hit trying to drive a real deploy
from an agent instead of a browser.

REPO WAS HARDCODED. GH_REPO is <owner>/cloud, baked into every call site.
The constellation's Android/APK ship workflows live in the unix monorepo,
so they were invisible to this MCP — not merely untriggerable, but absent
from gha, gha_ok and gha_errors as well. `repo` is now a parameter on all
seven tools. This was the real blocker; input support alone would have
changed nothing.

NO INPUTS. gha_trigger ran `gh workflow run` with no -f/--field, so a
workflow_dispatch input could never be sent and any input-gated workflow
was unreachable. Now inputs/ref/repo.

NO LIFECYCLE. A run could be seen but not retried, cancelled, or fetched
by id — and gha_errors only reaches 24h, so anything older meant leaving
the MCP for the web UI. Added gha_rerun (--failed by default, so a flake
does not re-pay for the whole matrix), gha_cancel (a run on the wrong ref
or a stuck matrix burning runner minutes), and gha_run_logs (one run by
id, tailed to 400 lines because a matrix log is megabytes).

Inputs are refused for a bulk 'all' trigger rather than silently dropped:
inputs are per-workflow by definition, and thirty workflows quietly
ignoring one reads as success while doing nothing. Input names are
validated against [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_-]* because gh parses a leading '-'
as a flag — execAsync passes an argv array, so there is no shell to
inject into, but flag injection is still real.

Typechecked against the real dependency tree: 9 pre-existing errors
before this change, 9 after, none in the added code. The workflows.ts one
is the long-standing safeRun return-type mismatch at line 26, shared with
finops.ts and vps-ops.ts and deliberately untouched.

NOTE: this widens what the bearer token can reach. The MCP's actual power
is still bounded by the gh token on the host — if that token cannot see
the unix repo, these parameters will return 'not found' rather than
acting.
